                                "sense_id": "3f250992-0ee0-3294-8e32-6297e5506d57",
                                "text": "A noble gentleman of Rhodes, on his marriage with Evadne, discovers' that the marriage had been brought about by the king, her paramour..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b7a125e-7875-4434-8f8e-ed16bfa94e64",
                                "sense_id": "3f250992-0ee0-3294-8e32-6297e5506d57",
                                "text": "\"My dear boy,\" said Lady Adeline, \"You mustn't call Mrs. Colquhoun by her Christian name.\" \"Christian!\" jeered Diavolo. \"Now, that is a good one! There's nothing Christian about Evadne. - - - Evadne - classical Evadne - was noted for her devotion to her husband, and distinguished herself finally on his funeral pyre - she ex-pyred there.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c88eed97-46cc-4283-9276-4ed7845773de",
                                "sense_id": "3f250992-0ee0-3294-8e32-6297e5506d57",
                                "text": "'Unusual name, Evadne Platt.' 'You think so?' Barnaby could afford to sound superior."
                            }
                        ]
